### digest/ANALYSIS.md 1-150 (C1, C10, C11, C12 partial)
- Examples: sewer fund $52.6M diverted over 9 FY, ~10% of SSC revenues (RM §1 L219-223); OpenGov transfers $1.6-2.8M trending (L234-239); ACFR statements as inputs (L246-250).
- FA L1 Fn2: ACFR 180pp PDF, OpenGov JS app, budget docs for reading not analysis. Resolution: JSON tidy/long core w/ provenance, locator, hash, criticality, fact/analysis/judgment classification (FA L156-163; TAD §7.1 l.693-696).
- FA L1 Fn3/TAD §7.2: dataset snapshot = raw capture + canonicalized normalized dataset (hashed, diffed) + rendered view; hash over normalized dataset; keyed to stable query definition.
- FA L2 Fn2 L271-281: cross-source reconciliation, budget vs actuals; significance judgment is human.
- FA L2 Fn3: facts verifiable, analysis reproducible, judgment debatable; classification travels.
- TAD §7.4: keyed field-level diff w/ numeric tolerances; change propagates re-eval flag.
- TAD §7.1: Tabula/Camelot for native PDFs; prefer source's published spreadsheet over re-parsing PDF.
- TAD §8.3: spreadsheets only as OUTPUT surface; TAD §9 bundle substrate "Never a spreadsheet". TAD §9 (retired stack) Python in sandbox for data.
- TAD §3 description-as-truth for SVG (charts). TAD §10.2 Mechanical Verification Law.
- SD §3 row 4: extents incl sheet-cell; row 5 sheet-range, doc-table landed FW-19; CSV format FW-23, dialect REC-218.
- AC §3 Consequence: computed from record or assessed by member; causation separate (consequences module). AC §4 r1 machine may compute, labelled; r3 no significance/score field.
- MS M2: Sheet1!B14 cell citation; MS M8 adminarith ops: tally computed not transcribed; MS M6 budget book 39.6MB, R2 custody unplanned.
- UK: interactive visuals in publications; printed version first-class.
- OLD: coverage % over subjects from the case; honest negatives (never_looked/undetermined/no_subjects); "zero of zero is not 100%"; tally viewer-independence; count discloses existence (BOB #15); reproducibility checked byte-for-byte.
- DIST: UNDETERMINED never a match; verdict pass/fail.
- PS: no single confidence score; no centrality; "a count is a volume proxy and volume is not meaning"; kappa easy to read as validity.
- CON Step 8a: satisfaction conditions evaluator (D-88), progress computed from record; CON header: budget-or-dataset type OWED, measured first (EBD §2).
- DEC-4: member must tell whether document said figure or machine guessed; digits where OCR fails. DEC-5: cross-document aggregation/facets over metadata. DEC-11: figure change $4.2M->$2.8M via tracked changes. DEC-14: causal inference refused; UNPROVEN a stated state. DEC-18 ungraded leg inert. DEC-21 capture vs connection grade not combined. GAP: grade system ranges over documents and edges only, no population for computed figure/dataset row/calculation step (C11).
