### Primary sources opened (step 5)
- build/requirements/consequences.md (whole, 90 lines): R2 computed {op, operands}; machine may record computed part labelled; Suggestions sheet-range/doc-table natural operand; budget reader belongs to extraction/docprofile. Status: "The record holds no amounts or fund figures as values".
- bio-plane/src/consequences/figures.mjs (whole, 93 lines): OPS sum/difference/count/product/ratio; FIGURE regex (no %); passageHolds = fold(text).includes(fold(figure)) — figure must appear ANYWHERE in passage text (not a cell position); count = operands.length; sum/diff to decimals; product/ratio 15 sig digits.
- consequences/index.mjs 230-300: #passageText via content.passageText.
- build/requirements/content.md (whole, 154 lines): R1 extents incl sheet-cell, sheet-range; R46 passageText → null when no unit at exactly that extent.
- content/index.mjs:1264 passageText; content/notice.mjs heldTextAt: "the record holds no text at exactly ... (only whole indexed units — a PDF page, a paragraph, a slide — carry text)". FINDING: a sheet-cell operand → passageText null → consequence part undetermined. reading-pipeline R15: one unit per SHEET (its used sheet-range) (D-672); unit capped 128 KiB (extraction R22) → large sheet truncated → null. So consequences' "natural operand" works only for (a) a whole-sheet range under 128 KiB, where passageHolds checks the figure appears anywhere in the sheet's tab-joined text (position not pinned), or (b) a member's typed transcription (content R24). The cell-level operand path is effectively unbuilt.
- build/requirements/office-readers.md 1-230: R10 formula envelope {kind:formula, source, formula, value}; R11 xlsx document tab-joined; sheets list; csv row 1 is row 1; R9 rangeUnits (defined names, tables); R12 20 MiB guard; R14 dialect; R17/R18 refs. No cell typing.
- build/modules.json: 98 entries; consequences layer 9 uses [... content, inquiry, strength, conformance]; used by filings, escalation, affordances, control-plane, plane. content used by 22 incl query-language, retrieval, inquiry. runtime-limits used by ai-runs, agent-worker...
- build/layers.md (whole, 274 lines): layer contracts; layer 5 "Everything derived over content, with its grade"; layer 9 consequences row; P17 ruling 5 amended: adding/removing product module or layer change → Bob; uses/order within layer/file ownership → BOB. accepted-work pattern (layer 6 registration facade filled by layer-8 case-import) — precedent for lower read of later data. case-checker: pure function + standalone offline program with readable format spec, recomputes grades at stated method version. Layer 7 Beyond MVP Discovery.
- build/requirements/runtime-limits.md (whole): Workers freeze Date.now during sync execution; counts not times; cpuProbe finds ceiling.
- journeys.html (design branch) journey 6 text confirmed (lines 154-165 of extracted text); §6 "Calculating over a dataset" row (line 369); police overtime/bond/budget/dataset front doors (60-75).
- intent.md R2-R5, Bounds (read): condition {progression, entity, relation, filter, required {grade, stages}, satisfied {share}}; only filter key evaluated = entity_kind; others -> undetermined; satisfied three-valued; >1,000 matched -> null. No amounts.
- case-checker.md (whole, 85 lines): pure checkCaseFile + standalone program (R13: one self-contained file, no install, no network, same build same bytes, carries own SHA-256); R5 grades recomputed by strength.recomputePair at stated version; UNKNOWN_METHOD_VERSION → missing; R16 same args same answer byte-identical on copy and standalone; Suggestions: import only pure code (strength/arithmetic.mjs). → TEMPLATE for calculation recompute.
- strength.md R31 GRADING_METHOD_VERSION changes whenever arithmetic changes; gradingMethodText complete enough to recompute by hand; R32 recomputePair answers for every published version; method.mjs: "live walk resolves each leg against the record and then composes here, and recomputePair resolves each leg from the case file's facts and composes here, so a grade recomputes the same by construction". → TEMPLATE.
- EXTRACTION-BREADTH-DESIGN.txt §2-§4 (lines 40-122): row 5 budget or dataset (two arms) and row 6 financial report (BOB #32: budget is plan; statement reports actuals; separate types); "No reader is written from this". §3.1 table structure in office = cells; PDF table(engine) derivation calibrated like OCR. §3.3 PDF tables NO-GO M-55. §4 EXTRACT productions incl "proposed table structure (once GO)", "cleaned/normalised text: derivation; NOT a transcription — a person supplies text, a machine only transforms it".
