### Web research (step 6)
- HyperFormula: GPLv3 or commercial (Handsontable); 380+ functions; Excel/Sheets syntax. https://hyperformula.handsontable.com/docs/ ; https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/hyperformula@3.2.0/README.md  → GPLv3 problematic for a group's instance? (GPL is fine to distribute w/ source; but product license? check repo license) — note.
- IronCalc: Rust, wasm, MIT/Apache-2.0, 300+ Excel-compatible functions, xlsx import/export; ironcalc_base embeddable. https://github.com/ironcalc/IronCalc
- ProPublica bulletproofing: raw file untouched copy, data log/journal, methodology, spot-checks. https://www.ire.org/?p=44398 ; https://www.propublica.org/nerds/what-i-learned-from-my-fellowship-at-propublica
- Socrata SoQL $group with $select aggregates sum/count/avg/min/max. https://dev.socrata.com/docs/queries/group
- Cloudflare Workers Paid: 128 MB memory per isolate; CPU 30 s default, max 5 min; subrequests 10,000; script 64 MiB. https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/platform/limits/
- DO SQLite: 10 GB/object; 100 columns/table; 2 MB max string/BLOB/row; 100 KB SQL statement; 100 bound params; 32 args/function; CPU 30 s/5 min. https://developers.cloudflare.com/durable-objects/platform/limits/
- GAO-20-283G Assessing Data Reliability (Dec 2019): accuracy, completeness, applicability; risk-based; report language. https://www.gao.gov/products/gao-20-283g
- GAGAS audit documentation: "sufficient detail to enable an experienced auditor, having no previous connection to the audit, to understand ... nature, timing, extent, and results of audit procedures performed; the evidence obtained; and its source and the conclusions reached". https://gaoinnovations.gov/yellowbook/2024/audit-documentation-1.html
- Reinhart-Rogoff: averaged rows 30-44 not 30-49; five countries excluded; 2.2% vs -0.1%; found by replication from the shared spreadsheet (Herndon, Ash, Pollin). https://retractionwatch.com/2013/04/18/influential-reinhart-rogoff-economics-paper-suffers-database-error/
- Panko: ~94% of field-audited spreadsheets have errors; cell error rate ~1-5% of formula cells. https://arxiv.org/pdf/0801.3114.pdf ; https://mba.tuck.dartmouth.edu/spreadsheet/product_pubs_files/Errors.pdf
- Ziemann 2016: ~1/5 of papers with Excel gene lists had autoconversion errors (704 articles). https://genomebiology.biomedcentral.com/track/pdf/10.1186/s13059-016-1044-7
- Frictionless Data: resource hash "sha256:..." in Data Package; Table Schema for field types. https://framework.frictionlessdata.io/docs/resources/table.html
- W3C CSVW (4 Recommendations, 17 Dec 2015): metadata vocabulary for tabular data, datatypes, cell level. https://www.w3.org/TR/tabular-metadata/
- Fiscal Data Package (Frictionless; OKI/GIFT/World Bank): columnTypes administrative/functional/economic classification code/label; phases Plan/Actual ("approved", "executed"). https://specs.frictionlessdata.io/fiscal-data-package/ ; https://fiscaltransparency.net/open-fiscal-data-package/
- FDTA (P.L. 117-263, Dec 2022): Phase 1 joint final rule published 8 June 2026; Phase 2 SEC deadline 1 Oct 2028; MSRB no deadline; compliance date unknown → machine-readable muni financial statements are years away. https://www.gfoa.org/fdta
- Datasette: SQLite publishing; canned queries; shareable query URLs; Baltimore Sun salaries. https://feeds.simonwillison.net/tags/datasette/?page=47 (weak source; prefer docs) 
- Datasette canned queries: named SQL in metadata with :params; shareable query URLs. https://docs.datasette.io/en/stable/sql_queries.html
- ArcGIS REST query: resultOffset/resultRecordCount paging, exceededTransferLimit, outStatistics, returnCountOnly (approximate counts in some cases). https://www.fairfaxcounty.gov/gisint1/rest/services/PLUS/PLUSGISRecords/FeatureServer/0/query?f=help
- CKAN DataStore: datastore_search (filters, q, limit, offset), datastore_search_sql (SELECT, aggregation). https://docs.ckan.org/en/ckan-2.1.5/datastore.html
- PDF tables: arXiv 2410.09871 compares Camelot, pdfplumber, PyMuPDF, Tabula, TATR; rule-based tools category-dependent; TATR best in Financial table detection; academic benchmark (2303.09957) Camelot F1 0.30, Tabula 0.28, Adobe 0.47. https://arxiv.org/abs/2410.09871 ; https://arxiv.org/pdf/2303.09957 — consistent with M-55 NO-GO.
- Formula.js MIT (Excel functions in JS). https://npmjs.com/package/formulajs
- The Markup Method: Build, Bulletproof, Show your work (datasets+code published). https://themarkup.org/about
- Vega-Lite: declarative JSON spec mapping data fields to channels → fits description-as-truth (SR §2.3). https://vega.github.io/vega-lite/ (via archive) / https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/research/?p=449646
- W3C PROV-O REC 30 Apr 2013: Entity/Activity/Agent; used, wasGeneratedBy, wasDerivedFrom. https://www.w3.org/TR/prov-o/
- OpenFormula ISO/IEC 26300-2:2015: interoperable recalculated formulas "will produce equivalent results if given equivalent inputs". https://www.iso.org/standard/88132.html (search result)
- SheetJS CE Apache 2.0; cell .v .w .t .f. https://git.sheetjs.com/It/sheetjs (search result)
- DuckDB-Wasm: in-process analytical SQL in browser/Node, CSV/Parquet/JSON. https://duckdb.org/2021/10/29/duckdb-wasm.html
- Spreadsheet engines differ: IEEE-754 doubles; Excel "close to zero" heuristic inconsistently applied (SUM); LibreOffice accumulates rounding. https://exceljet.net/articles/floating-point-errors-in-excel ; https://help.libreoffice.org/latest/om/text/scalc/01/calculation_accuracy.html
- OpenGov/Socrata (Tyler Data & Insights) budget platforms; exports CSV; Socrata Open Budget. https://www.route-fifty.com/digital-government/2016/02/machine-readable-budget-in-a-human-friendly-format/299552/
- Audit attribute sampling: confidence 90/95/99%, tolerable exception rate, expected exception; proportions near 0/1 need exact intervals. https://ww2.amstat.org/meetings/proceedings/2019/data/assets/pdf/1199463.pdf ; https://rdrr.io/cran/PracTools/man/nAuditAttr.html
- Repo facts: bio-plane has NO runtime npm dependencies (devDependencies only: miniflare, wrangler, esbuild); ocr-worker vendors tesseract-wasm 0.11.0 as a separate layer-1 Worker (fleet member) — precedent for a vendored wasm engine in its own Worker.
- case-checker code present (bio-plane/src/case-checker/: check.mjs, program.mjs...), 29/29 tests (K1412).
- rulings.md: no K ruling on calculation/spreadsheet/dataset (grep empty).
### Synthesis plan (step 7 started)
